  "title": "The Comet Tail Repair Shop",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "fantasy and science fiction",
  "premise": "A mechanic must repair a comet’s tangled decorative tail before a parade, but brushing it straight removes every playful curl. They arrange the curls into a deliberate spiral ribbon, attach a tiny parade bell, and send the comet off with its unusual tail proudly intact.",
  "hook": "Your tail is not broken. It is badly introduced.",
  "visible_action": "Comet parks at a tiny bay; tail knots loosen; curls spring back; ribbon forms a spiral; comet glides away trailing the new pattern.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A repair can preserve character rather than erase it.",
  "gate": "Personified decorative comet; no claim about real comet composition, trajectories, or repair.",
